\f1\fs22 \'93Agent Jones made contact, High Elvis.\'94 Holy Aunt Hayley, police duties making her late as usual, drifted into the committee room holding her notepad and read the message. \'93He says, \'91Director Hardman will require a 6 piece Elvis band to play a gig at the Gravity Well Lounge, Penthouse Level Hardy Tower One. Thursday 25 June at 7.00pm.\'92 Agent Jones has, in effect, asked us to send in some sacrificial lambs. Now we decide who we offer up.\'94\
\'93We now have a crack team of operatives that could intercede.\'94 The Minister for Graceland Security proudly announced. \
\'93Director Hardman has arranged the gig in The Gravity Well for a reason. It\'92s deep in L.5. territory and the security is too tight. I guarantee they will be there in numbers and geared up for a slaughter. We will never be able to sneak in enough back-up to take them all. I do not think we have to intercede, in fact I suggest that we do nothing at all.\'94 As she spoke the faces of the cabinet became ashen, but as she continued the cabinet became stolid and unified with resolve. \'93They must have their lab rats to experiment on. I would therefore suggest we ready ourselves to innoculate with the T-virus, but only do so after we have our volunteers.\'94\

